    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Fixed layout — where the coordinates come from",
      "gridPos": { "h": 7, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 0 },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "# Fixed layout\n\nFixed layout draws each Graph node at a saved x and y position. You can supply positions with `fixedx` and `fixedy` node fields. You can also set `Fixed x` and `Fixed y` for a node with field overrides.\n\nIf a node does not have both coordinates, the panel places it on a stable ring. If some nodes have coordinates, the ring surrounds those nodes. A dashboard reload keeps the same fallback positions.\n\nUse a practical coordinate range, such as pixel values. A range from 0 to 1 can offset horizontal or vertical links from their nodes.\n\nPanels 1 and 4 enable Draggable nodes. Drag a node to save the displayed positions as field overrides."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "grafana-echarts-relations-panel",
      "title": "1 · Fixed, nothing pinned — every node seeded",
      "description": "The edge-only query does not provide node coordinates. The panel places all four nodes on a ring in data order. Reload the dashboard to see that the fallback positions stay the same. Draggable nodes is on, so you can move a node.",
      "datasource": { "type": "grafana-testdata-datasource" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 12, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 7 },
      "fieldConfig": { "defaults": { "color": { "mode": "palette-classic" } }, "overrides": [] },
      "options": {
